  <h1>Exchange Program</h1>
  <p>
    In the fall of 2024, I attended the University of Michigan's School of
    Information, immersing myself in a diverse curriculum that bridged the
    technical, ethical, and communicative aspects of information science.
  </p>
  <p>
    I developed practical skills in building data-driven web applications with
    Django and Python. In "Automotive UX," I explored user experience design
    within the automotive industry, gaining insights into in-car interface
    development. "Introduction to Information Ethics" provided a framework for
    evaluating the ethical implications of information technologies, while
    "Intro to Project Management" equipped me with tools for managing
    non-repetitive business activities. I also strengthened my communication
    skills through courses like "Interactive Communication" and "Editing and
    Style."
  </p>
  <p>
    This experience broadened my perspective on information science and deepened
    my ability to approach problems from multiple disciplines.
  </p>
